ersity and inclusion Indigenous engagement Climate and sustainability Back to home Home About Mta Work At Mta Current Opportunities Part-time Lecturer - Department Of Classics Part-time Lecturer - Department of Classics Department: Department of Classics Opportunity type: Academic (part-time) Position title: Part-time Lecturer - Department of Classics Classification: Part-time lecturer Supervisor's title: Department Head Posted date: August 26, 2026 Closing date: October 5, 2026 Position description The Department of Classics at Mount Allison University invites applications for a stipendiary appointment to teach the following course during the Winter term of the 2026–2027 academic year: LATI 1101: Introductory Latin II Preference will be given to applicants who: Are available to teach the course in person; Hold a PhD in Classics or a closely related field; Have prior university-level teaching experience. The course involves three hours of in-person instruction per week. While in-person teaching is preferred, the university may consider offering this course online if necessary. The anticipated enrolment is between 10 and 15 students. The successful candidate will receive a stipend of $8,490 for the term of the appointment. Applicants should submit a curriculum vitae that includes the names and contact information of three academic referees. Applications should be submitted electronically to: Dr. Ilaria Battiloro Head, Department of Classics Mount Allison University 63D York St. Sackville, NB E4L 1G9 Email: ibattiloro@mta.ca Review of applications will begin on October 5, 2026. Social Media Facebook Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Helpful Links Athletics Employment Events News and the Record For media For employers and partners For contractors, vendors, and suppliers Contact Information Campus map Safety and security Urgent assistance and crisis support Directory Mailing address: Mount Allison University Sackville , New Brunswick Canada E4L 1E4 We would like to acknowledge