rsity and inclusion Indigenous engagement Climate and sustainability Back to home Home About Mta Work At Mta Current Opportunities Part-time Lecturer - Department Of Biology Part-time Lecturer - Department of Biology Department: Department of Biology Opportunity type: Academic (part-time) Position title: Part-time Lecturer - Department of Biology Classification: Part-time lecturer Salary range: $8,490 stipend for the term Supervisor's title: Department Head Posted date: July 30, 2026 Closing date: August 14, 2026 Position description The Department of Biology at Mount Allison University invites applications for a part-time stipendiary position for the winter 2027 session. We are seeking someone to teach BIOL 3991B: Animal Health. The course format will be in-person and will be a 3-credit hour course spanning 13 weeks that will serve approximately 20-24 undergraduate students. Applicants should possess a PhD and have extensive experience teaching Animal Health at the university level. Applicants should also have a strong commitment to undergraduate teaching. Applicants should include a cover letter outlining their relevant experience and a curriculum vitae to: Dr. Karen Crosby Chair of the Search Committee Department of Biology Mount Allison University 63B York Street Sackville, NB, E4L 1G7 Email: kcrosby@mta.ca Applications must be received by August 14, 2026 Social Media Facebook Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Helpful Links Athletics Employment Events News and the Record For media For employers and partners For contractors, vendors, and suppliers Contact Information Campus map Safety and security Urgent assistance and crisis support Directory Mailing address: Mount Allison University Sackville , New Brunswick Canada E4L 1E4 We would like to acknowledge that we are located within the territory of Mi’kma’ki, the unceded, ancestral territory of the Mi’kmaq. Our relationship and our privilege to live on this territory was agreed upon in the Peace and Friendship Treaties of