ity and inclusion Indigenous engagement Climate and sustainability Back to home Home About Mta Work At Mta Current Opportunities Part-time Lecturer - Department Of Music Part-time Lecturer - Department of Music Department: Department of Music Opportunity type: Academic (part-time) Position title: Part-time Lecturer - Department of Music Classification: Part-time lecturer Supervisor's title: Department Head Posted date: May 29, 2026 Closing date: June 12, 2026 Anticipated start date: January 1, 2027 Position description The Music Department at Mount Allison University invites applications for the position of Director of the Mount Allison Chamber Orchestra (MUSC 1639-4639) and Symphonic Band (MUSC 1639-4639). This is a stipendiary (part-time) appointment. Preference will be given to applicants with degrees and/or diplomas in performance or conducting and an established record of successful ensemble direction at the university and professional levels. Responsibilities include directing rehearsals, evaluating student participation, and preparing up to two public concerts per ensemble. These positions are for the Winter term only: January 2027 to April 2027. Rehearsals will be held on the campus of Mount Allison University. The Chamber Orchestra rehearses once a week on Thursday evenings from 7:00 to 9:30 pm. The Symphonic Band rehearses twice a week on Monday and Wednesday evenings from 6:00 to 7:30 pm. Candidates should clearly indicate in their application materials which of the above courses they are applying for. Application materials should be sent to the email address below and should include: a letter of interest a curriculum vitae a short teaching philosophy statement recordings of recent performances (ideally of ensemble direction, if available) names and contact information of at least two referees Dr. Kevin Morse Head and Chair of Search Committee Department of Music Mount Allison University 134 Main Street Sackville, NB, E4L 1A6 Email: kmorse@mta.ca Review of applications will begin on June 12, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Social Media Facebook Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Helpful Links Athletics Employment Events News and the Record For media For employers and partners For contractors, vendors, and suppliers Contact Information Campus map Safety and security Urgent assistance and crisis support Directory Mailing address: Mount Allison University Sackville , New Brunswick Canada E4L 1E4 We would like to acknowledge that we are located within the territory of Mi’kma’ki, the unceded, ancestral territory of the Mi’kmaq. Our relationship and our privilege to live on this territory was agreed upon in the Peace and Friendship Treaties of 1752. Because of this treaty relationship it is to be acknowledged that we are all Treaty people and have a responsibility to respect this territory. Copyright © 2026 Mount Allison University Legal Menu Privacy Terms of use Accessibility"
