ity and inclusion Indigenous engagement Climate and sustainability Back to home Home About Mta Work At Mta Current Opportunities Part-time Lecturer - Department Of Music Part-time Lecturer - Department of Music Department: Department of Music Opportunity type: Academic (part-time) Position title: Part-time Lecturer - Department of Music Classification: Part-time lecturer Supervisor's title: Department Head Posted date: May 29, 2026 Closing date: June 12, 2026 Anticipated start date: September 1, 2026 Position description The Music Department at Mount Allison University invites applications for the position of instructor in Organ. This is a stipendiary (part-time) appointment. Preference will be given to applicants with graduate degrees in organ performance, an established record as a performer, and studio teaching experience at the university level. Teaching responsibilities include weekly studio instruction for one student (MUSC 1501-4591), approximately 1 hour per week plus studio class, overseeing student performance preparation, and assessing performance juries for this student. These courses run for both Fall and Winter semesters: September 2026 to April 2027. These courses will be taught on the campus of Mount Allison University. Application materials should be sent to the email address below and should include: a letter of interest a curriculum vitae a short teaching philosophy statement a link to a short teaching demonstration video (this is optional; up to 10 minutes; may be a video of in-person or online one-on-one teaching) links to recordings of recent solo performances (please indicate dates of recordings) names and contact information of at least two referees Dr. Kevin Morse Head and Chair of Search Committee Department of Music Mount Allison University 134 Main Street Sackville, NB, E4L 1A6 Email: kmorse@mta.ca Review of applications will begin on June 12, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Social Media Facebook Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Helpful Links Athletics Employment Events News and the Record For media For employers and partners For contractors, vendors, and suppliers Contact Information Campus map Safety and security Urgent assistance and crisis support Directory Mailing address: Mount Allison University Sackville , New Brunswick Canada E4L 1E4 We would like to acknowledge that we are located within the territory of Mi’kma’ki, the unceded, ancestral territory of the Mi’kmaq. Our relationship and our privilege to live on this territory was agreed upon in the Peace and Friendship Treaties of 1752. Because of this treaty relationship it is to be acknowledged that we are all Treaty people and have a responsibility to respect this territory. Copyright © 2026 Mount Allison University Legal Menu Privacy Terms of use Accessibility"
